WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:06.964
Pollyanna steered Jimmy Bean straight into Aunt Polly's sitting room.

2
00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:12.848
"Oh, Aunt Polly! I have something even nicer than Fluffy and Buffy for you to bring up.

3
00:00:12.849 --> 00:00:18.405
A real live boy!" Pollyanna smiled broadly.

4
00:00:18.406 --> 00:00:23.132
"He won't mind sleeping in the attic at first, and he says he'll work.

5
00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:27.631
But I'll need him most of the time to play with me."

6
00:00:27.632 --> 00:00:36.144
"Pollyanna!" Aunt Polly's face turned white with shock and then red with anger.

7
00:00:36.145 --> 00:00:43.216
"Who is this dirty little boy? Where did you find him?"

8
00:00:43.217 --> 00:00:48.192
Jimmy hesitated and looked toward the door, but Pollyanna pressed on.

9
00:00:48.193 --> 00:00:51.617
"He is dirty, but I'm sure he'll improve with a bath.

10
00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:58.858
Just like Fluffy and Buffy did! He's an orphan, and his name is Jimmy Bean."

11
00:00:58.859 --> 00:01:01.915
"But what is he doing here?"

12
00:01:01.916 --> 00:01:06.554
"I just explained why he's here," Pollyanna said patiently.

13
00:01:06.555 --> 00:01:10.025
"Jimmy wants a home and a family.

14
00:01:10.026 --> 00:01:14.157
I told him how good you were to Buffy and Fluffy and me.

15
00:01:14.158 --> 00:01:18.174
And that you'd take him in too."

16
00:01:18.175 --> 00:01:22.416
Aunt Polly sat down and raised a shaking hand to her throat.

17
00:01:22.417 --> 00:01:26.655
The familiar helplessness was threatening to overcome her again.

18
00:01:26.656 --> 00:01:29.570
But she suddenly sat up straight.

19
00:01:29.571 --> 00:01:35.219
"Pollyanna, this is the most absurd thing you've done yet," Aunt Polly said.

20
00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:40.635
"As if mangy dogs and cats weren't bad enough, you bring home a ragged little beggar who—"

21
00:01:40.636 --> 00:01:44.407
Jimmy's eyes flashed with anger as he confronted Aunt Polly.

22
00:01:44.408 --> 00:01:48.856
"I'm not a beggar, and I don't want anything from you!"

23
00:01:48.857 --> 00:01:53.043
He stood right in front of her with his hands on his hips.

24
00:01:53.044 --> 00:01:58.161
"I'm willing to work, but I wouldn't have come to your old house if this girl hadn't made me.

25
00:01:58.162 --> 00:02:03.212
She said you were so good and kind—the nicest lady in the world.

26
00:02:03.213 --> 00:02:07.787
She also said you would be glad to have me live here."

27
00:02:07.788 --> 00:02:13.762
As Pollyanna watched helplessly, Jimmy stormed from the room.

28
00:02:13.763 --> 00:02:19.109
"Oh, Aunt Polly, I thought you would be glad to have Jimmy—"

29
00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:22.773
Aunt Polly raised her hand to silence Pollyanna.

30
00:02:22.774 --> 00:02:31.414
She felt herself wavering as she remembered Jimmy calling her "good and kind." But then she rallied.

31
00:02:31.415 --> 00:02:36.159
"Pollyanna, please stop using that word glad

32
00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:41.452
. All I hear is glad, glad, glad until I can't take it anymore!"

33
00:02:41.453 --> 00:02:44.901
Pollyanna's jaw dropped in amazement.

34
00:02:44.902 --> 00:02:51.370
"Why, Aunt Polly, I'd think you'd be glad to have me feel gl—oh!"

35
00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:55.146
She broke off suddenly and ran from the room.

36
00:02:55.147 --> 00:02:59.377
Before Jimmy reached the end of the driveway, Pollyanna overtook him.

37
00:02:59.378 --> 00:03:07.286
"Wait! I'm so sorry!" Pollyanna was panting as she held out her hand to him.

38
00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:11.793
"Please don't blame Aunt Polly—she really is good and kind.

39
00:03:11.794 --> 00:03:17.633
It's my fault because I didn't do a good job of introducing you."

40
00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:22.965
"I'm not blaming you." Jimmy shrugged and turned away.

41
00:03:22.966 --> 00:03:28.395
"I guess I can find my own place to live. But I'm no beggar!"

42
00:03:28.396 --> 00:03:32.535
"I do wish I could find someplace for you, though."

43
00:03:32.536 --> 00:03:37.602
Pollyanna was looking at Jimmy thoughtfully when she suddenly got a bright idea.

44
00:03:37.603 --> 00:03:42.242
"I know what I'll do! The Ladies' Aid meets this afternoon at Aunt Polly's church.

45
00:03:42.243 --> 00:03:47.842
I'll tell them all about you." Pollyanna was excited about her plan.

46
00:03:47.843 --> 00:03:53.998
"That's what Father always did whenever he wanted anything for his church."

47
00:03:53.999 --> 00:03:58.324
"Oh, no!" Jimmy backed away from Pollyanna.

48
00:03:58.325 --> 00:04:02.535
"It's bad enough having one lady call me a beggar.

49
00:04:02.536 --> 00:04:08.582
I'm not standing around and listening to a whole room full of ladies call me that."

50
00:04:08.583 --> 00:04:15.326
"But you wouldn't be there. I'd go by myself, and I'd tell your story better this time."

51
00:04:15.327 --> 00:04:19.986
Pollyanna kept talking as she sensed Jimmy changing his mind.

52
00:04:19.987 --> 00:04:24.638
"I'm sure someone there would be glad to give you a home."

53
00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:31.221
"I'm willing to work," Jimmy reminded her. "Don't forget to say that."

54
00:04:31.222 --> 00:04:35.535
"Of course not. Then tomorrow I'll tell you what happened.

55
00:04:35.536 --> 00:04:39.392
I'll meet you on the road where I found you this morning."

56
00:04:39.393 --> 00:04:45.539
Jimmy promised to be there and said he'd decided to return to the Orphans' Home for the night.

57
00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:49.992
"Even though I don't think they'd miss me," he added.

58
00:04:49.993 --> 00:04:54.374
"They aren't like a family, you know."

59
00:04:54.375 --> 00:05:00.036
"I do know," Pollyanna said sympathetically.

60
00:05:00.037 --> 00:05:06.125
Meanwhile Aunt Polly was watching the children from her sitting room window.

61
00:05:06.126 --> 00:05:11.557
She kept remembering Jimmy saying scornfully that she was so good and kind.

62
00:05:11.558 --> 00:05:19.866
And Aunt Polly felt sad, as if she'd lost something.

